# Do not run the process

The user runs this project. The agent does not.

Do not start `batch_process.py`, `main.py`, `orquestrador.py`, `routes.py`, or any other command that loads data, connects to Oracle, or runs the solver. Do not launch those commands to "verify", "see the logs", or "try it".

"We are going to execute", "we will run", and "let's execute it" mean the user will run it. Stay put. Answer the question. Do not touch the terminal for a run.

Run a process only when the current message explicitly orders that run, for example "run the batch now" or "execute the process". A plan to run later is not that order.

Reading code, editing code, and answering questions do not require a run.
